# Canonical .gitattributes for fleet repos.
#
# Copy to the repo root as `.gitattributes` (note the leading dot — this
# reference file is stored without it so it isn't itself active in fleet-kit).
#
# Why this exists: on a mixed Windows/Linux fleet with Linux CI, a developer's
# core.autocrlf can check files out with CRLF. Prettier (endOfLine: lf) then
# reports those files as "would reformat" locally, even though they are LF in
# git and pass on Linux CI — a false "format debt" that nearly triggers an
# unnecessary reformat. Forcing LF in the working copy makes local == CI.
# See fleet/lessons/2026-07-24-crlf-vs-linux-ci.md.

# Normalize everything to LF in the repo; let git decide text vs binary.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell stays platform-native (Windows tooling tolerates both, and some
# PS hosts prefer CRLF).
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Explicit binaries — never touch line endings or diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# --- repo-specific additions below ---

# OpenAPI spec snapshots come from GitHub raw with LF endings; locking
# them prevents CRLF round-trip noise on Windows checkouts so diffs
# from re-fetching stay reviewable. (Subsumed by the `* text=auto eol=lf`
# rule above, kept explicit because the intent is not obvious.)
docs/specs/*.json text eol=lf
